    "created_at": "2016-01-27T23:36:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-27T23:36:39Z",
    "body": "> When `source` is in `template`, should `template`'s content model be decided based on the attributes of the first `source` element? Like, if it has a `srcset` attribute, use the `picture` content model; otherwise use the `video`/`audio` content model.\n\nAfter thinking about this, that makes sense to me (though I think it’s going to be complicated to implement in the checker). But maybe this is a case where we ideally need some real use cases if we can find them—examples from actual web developers who are using `source` within `template`. I wonder if @studdugie  might have some feedback on this.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
